Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(layout): let an end-aligned pair drag fall through to
 the cross axis

The interior trailing branch returned once it had set both lane widths, so a
corner drag (RIGHT|BOTTOM) applied only dx and silently ignored dy. The pair
case now takes the else arm of the primary-end path and the cross-axis block
runs as it does for every other edge combination.

Pinned by a two-window column drag that asserts both the width trade and the
height split; restoring the return reds only the cross-axis assertions.

